  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1057 AM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nUpper-level and surface ridging will remain in place through the \nmiddle to end of this week before the next system approaches the \narea Saturday into Sunday. The upper ridge will be slow to shift \neast, even as the aformentioned system approaches for the weekend. \nThis will keep dry conditions and light winds in place and will also \nact to weaken the approaching system. In fact, the limited return \nmoisture with very limited moisture available from the Gulf, will \nkeep precipitation amounts and rain chances at a minimum (20-30%). \nThe guidance continues to trend lower with overall rainfall amounts. \nTemperatures will trend above normal with the upper ridging and \nample sunshine across the Quad State. In fact, highs are expected to \nbe in the upper 60s to around 70 for the end of the week into the \nweekend. For comparison, normal high temperatures are in the upper \n50s for this time of year.\n\nBeyond the weekend, into Thanksgiving week, the ridge will weaken \nand temperatures are expected to trend closer to normal. There are \nsome signs of another system approaching late Monday into Tuesday of \nnext week, but it is only worth mentioning at this point as there is \na large amount of uncertainty.",
